  "serialized": [
   "Directly after the code, each resource has a table of 73 (slot data offset, source data offset) pairs (header word 56 is the count). Source offsets point at record payloads in the data area: 58 text records (tunable and section names), 11 empty records (lengths (1, 1), payload 0) and four records with lengths (1, 1) whose 4-byte payload is non-zero.",
   "Entries 3 to 6 bind slots 0x550, 0x558, 0x560, 0x568 to those four records, whose payloads are the ids of Ability_SupportTrait, Ability_Commando_Base, Ability_MedicalTriage and Ability_SwiftTriage in that order. Same rows on 1.4.3.5 (source offsets 4 lower).",
   "The four slots are zero in the file, have no entry in the source asset's import list (imports bind 1352 and 1392 on either side) and are named by no code operand other than the four HasUpgrade? calls.",
   "Firing step (2.1.1.0 listing): 1d38 328a61dd(d280) -> prev; 1f30 target = firing ? 0.8 : 1; 1f54 5db3c702(...) -> x; 1f88 ffe1e419(60, x, 0.1) -> k; 1fb4 2ae5ca1e(prev, target, k) -> v; 241c output = m * v; 2464 47be3d90(d280) <- v.",
   "Other uses in the 1.4.3.5 listings: 2ae5ca1e appears 12 times, always (end value, end value, variable), including (1, 2, t) and (2, 1, t) in the same Igla graph. ffe1e419 appears 6 times, always with 60 first; in SimEx_SoldierMaster (59cc) its second argument is the frame-time function c58d8ea6 (DT?) directly, and at RootLayerLogic 5210-523c its result is divided by the same second argument."
